+const BASH_TOOL_DESCRIPTION_SUFFIX: &str = "- IMPORTANT: Do not send very large commands, inline scripts, or heredocs. If a command would exceed 100 lines or ~8000 characters, first create the script file with chunked write/edit calls, then run a short command that executes it.";
+const OPENCODE_WRITE_TOOL_DESCRIPTION_SUFFIX: &str = "- IMPORTANT: Each call must stay under 300 lines (~15000 characters) of content. For larger files, write the first 300 lines ending with a unique placeholder line, then use the edit tool to replace that placeholder with the next chunk (plus a new placeholder), repeating until done; the final chunk removes the placeholder. Do not attempt to write everything at once.";
+const OPENCODE_EDIT_TOOL_DESCRIPTION_SUFFIX: &str = "- IMPORTANT: Keep each `newString` under 300 lines (~15000 characters). Split larger changes into multiple edit calls; when appending, keep a unique placeholder line and replace it chunk by chunk.";
